(iv) NAND Gate
This is an AND gate followed by a NOT gate. If inputs A and B are both
‘1’, the output Y is not ‘1’. The gate gets its name from this NOT AND
behaviour. Figure 14.40 shows the symbol and truth table of NAND gate. NAND gates are also called Universal Gates since by using these
gates you can realise other basic gates like OR, AND and NOT (Exercises
14.16 and 14.17). FIGURE 14.40 (a) Logic symbol, (b) Truth table of NAND gate. Example 14.13 Sketch the output Y from a NAND gate having inputs
A and B given below:
